== Effects ==
* Grants [[spectral]] tears.
* When tears travel off-screen, they loop back around through the opposite wall.
* {{dlc|nr}} +2.25 [[range]].
* {{dlc|r}} +3 [[range]].
* {{dlc|nr}} +1.5 [[tear falling speed]].

== Notes ==
* {{dlc+|r+}} This item has a 1% chance to drop when defeating {{e|Mega Maw}}.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc+|r}} When fighting {{E|The Beast}} tears will not loop downward identical to a {{R|Crawl Space}}.{{dlc-}}

== Synergies ==
* {{Dlc|r}}{{C|Azazel}} / {{I|Brimstone}} / {{I|Revelation|n}} / {{C|Tainted Azazel}} / {{i|Technology}}: The laser continues behind Isaac and back once again, potentially hitting enemies twice in one blast.
* {{i|Bob's Rotten Head|nr}}: Bob's Rotten Head can travel through walls and appear out of the opposite wall.
** {{dlc|r}} Does not travel through the wall; instead bounces off it like with {{i|Rubber Cement}}.
* {{dlc|a+}} {{C|The Forgotten}}: The skeleton form's charge attack can loop through walls.
* {{i|A Lump of Coal}}: Tears will continually gain damage when passing through walls.
* {{i|Mom's Knife}}: Causes Mom's Knife to appear on the opposite wall if thrown through one. It then returns through the wall to Isaac.
** '''Mom's Knife''' + '''Brimstone''': The barrage of knives flies across the room until it hits the wall twice.
* {{i|My Reflection}}: When shooting through a wall, tears speed up towards Isaac rather than returning through the original wall. With enough [[shot speed]] and [[range]] the tears can loop twice.
* {{i|Tech X}}: Laser rings will go through walls, extra distance depending on [[shot speed]].
** {{dlc|nr}} '''Tech X''' + {{i|Incubus}}: Incubus's laser rings cannot go through walls. This applies to {{C|Lilith}} too.
** {{Dlc|r}} '''Tech X''' + {{i|Incubus}}: Laser rings travel through walls and continue on the other side of the room.
* {{i|Tractor Beam}}: Causes the tears to loop right back in front of Isaac after they go offscreen.

== Interactions ==
* {{dlc|nr}} {{i|Brimstone}}: Overrides Continuum, stat effects apply.
* {{dlc+|a+nr}} {{i|Compound Fracture}}: Tears will only split when hitting obstacles or enemies but not walls.{{dlc-}}
** {{Dlc|r}} Tears will split on contact with walls. Only one split will occur on contact with walls and objects.
* {{i|Dr. Fetus}}: Bombs cannot go through walls, but are spectral.
* {{i|Epic Fetus}} / {{i|Rubber Cement}}: Overrides Continuum, stat effects apply.
* {{i|The Ludovico Technique}}: When the tear is moved offscreen, it loops back through the opposite wall.
* {{dlc+|nr}} {{i|The Parasite}}: Tears will only split when hitting obstacles or enemies but not walls.{{dlc-}}
** {{Dlc|r}} Tears will split on contact with walls. Only one split will occur on contact with walls and objects.
* {{i|Proptosis}}: Tears shrink while traveling through walls and often disappear before they can reappear on the other side.
* {{i|Technology Zero}}: Tears will travel through walls; however, the electricity will not connect the tears while they are outside the room. Once tears have passed through walls, the electric arcs connect very erratically to other tears.
* {{i|Tiny Planet}}: Tears that travel through walls will travel until they reach Isaac and start orbiting him again.

